body:
Using a ruler and a pair of compasses **only**:

(a) construct $\triangle PQR$ such that angle $PQR = 90^\circ$, $|PQ| = 5.5$ cm and $|QR| = 8$ cm;

(b) construct a perpendicular of $\overline{PR}$ from $Q$;

(c) locate $M$, the intersection of the perpendicular and $\overline{PR}$;

(d) measure: (i) $|MR|$; (ii) $|QM|$;

(e) calculate, correct to the **nearest** whole number, the area of triangle $QMR$.

In your answer, give your two measurements and the area.

answer:
The slope of $F = \dfrac{9}{5}C + 32$ is $\dfrac{9}{5} = 1.8$.

> [!answer]
> {{green:For every rise of 1 $^\circ$C, the temperature in Fahrenheit rises by $\dfrac{9}{5}$ (1.8) $^\circ$F.}}
